  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If we take $f(x)=4 x^{4}$, then\r\n(i) $f(x)$ is continuous in (-2,2)\r\n(ii) $f(x)$ is differentiable in (-2,2)\r\n(iii) $f(-2)=f(2)$ So, $f(x)=4 x^{4}$ satisfies all the conditions of Rolle's theorem therefore $\\exists$ a point $c$ such that\r\n$f^{\\prime}(c)=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 16 c^{3}=0 \\Rightarrow c=0 \\in(-2,2)$",
    "image": null
  },
